    "done_when": "all four of these hold: The document answers the first question with a file and line for every path that acts on a deadline, and with the resolved fences.enforce_budget_watchdog of every mounted project. It answers the second with a table per lane: runs; median gate share of wall time over the runs whose every gate duration came from a log; the same median over every run with a measurable share, with the share of runs that used the tool-call fallback; the runs with no measurable share, each listed by id; runs with a truncated gate, each listed by id; and runs whose gate ran in the background, each listed by id. Every figure is read at a stated time, from streams and logs it names by count and date range. Both scanners are shown to see a known positive. The deadline scan reports _apply_budget_watchdog as a path that can act. The timing scan, run on r-20261018T084035535944-a-paired-arm-review-names-its-run, measures that run's after-arm gate within 5% of the 543 s its own log records (gate-after.log, \"in 543.02s\"). The document names the script and the command that produced every figure, and no file outside the write paths changes.",
